1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,792
Now the part that makes this system different: the loop.

2
00:00:04,792 --> 00:00:07,189
Every morning OROS proposes.

3
00:00:07,189 --> 00:00:17,715
Every evening it grades its own call, journals the verdict, and adjusts its own risk before it is allowed to propose again.

4
00:00:17,715 --> 00:00:21,652
Inside the book today: 6 positions up, 6 down.

5
00:00:21,652 --> 00:00:24,048
Best, CASY at +3.88 percent.

6
00:00:24,048 --> 00:00:25,845
Worst, SBUX at -2.66.

7
00:00:25,845 --> 00:00:30,809
Both go in the journal — wins and losses get the same ink.

8
00:00:30,809 --> 00:00:37,826
The honest scoreboard reads: expectancy -8.37% per trade over 83 graded positions.

9
00:00:37,826 --> 00:00:44,844
Because that record is soft, the system has throttled itself to 25% position size.

10
00:00:44,844 --> 00:00:49,979
Nobody told it to — full size must be earned back with wins.

11
00:00:49,979 --> 00:01:02,302
What tonight's read hands to tomorrow's open: 263 names close the day in Stage 2; position size stays cut to 25% until the record earns it back.

12
00:01:02,276 --> 00:01:09,611
All figures are simulated paper trading, graded and journaled by the OROS agents with no human intervention.

13
00:01:09,611 --> 00:01:11,852
Nothing here is financial advice.

14
00:01:11,852 --> 00:01:14,841
From the closing desk — see you at the open.
